<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Plan the work</span><p>Use the event kit and existing designs before briefing anything new.</p></div><a href="https://jira.skatelescope.org/servicedesk/customer/portal/364" class="button">Ask the Comms helpdesk <span class="arr arr-out" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><section class="kit" id="event-kit" data-kit><h2>The event kit</h2><p>Branded kit you can use for your event. Ask through the Comms helpdesk with your dates and where it needs to go. The Events and Logistics teams deliver it, including between sites.</p><ul class="kit-grid"><li class="kit-item"><div class="kit-pic" data-kit-image="kit-fabrilux-3m" data-shape="wide"></div><h3>Fabrilux backdrop, 3 m</h3><p class="kit-size">3 m wide, lit from inside</p><p>The main backdrop for a stand or press area. Three designs.</p></li><li class="kit-item"><div class="kit-pic" data-kit-image="kit-fabrilux-2m" data-shape="square"></div><h3>Fabrilux backdrop, 2 m</h3><p class="kit-size">2 m wide, lit from inside</p><p>On its own or beside the 3 m backdrop. Four designs.</p></li><li class="kit-item"><div class="kit-pic" data-kit-image="kit-pull-up-banners" data-shape="tall"></div><h3>Pull-up banners</h3><p class="kit-size">85 × 200 cm</p><p>Quick for one person to put up. Science Working Group designs and more, for talks, desks and side stages.</p></li><li class="kit-item"><div class="kit-pic" data-kit-image="kit-kiosk" data-shape="square"></div><h3>Kiosk</h3><p class="kit-size">1 m wide, lit from inside</p><p>A lit counter for a stand. Two styles, one with a worktop.</p></li><li class="kit-item"><div class="kit-pic" data-kit-image="kit-table-cloths" data-shape="cloth"></div><h3>Table cloths</h3><p class="kit-size">For a standard exhibition table</p><p>White or gradient, with the SKAO logo.</p></li></ul><p class="kit-care">Each banner travels in its own case with everything needed to put it up, and the Events Production Manual shows every step. Roll the fabric rather than folding it, and plug the lights into an approved power supply.</p></section><div data-downloads-slot hidden></div><section class="reading-section"><h2>Existing designs to reuse</h2><ul><li>SKAO apparel, promotional items, stationery and stickers.</li><li>SRCNet apparel.</li></ul><p>Ask for the artwork before briefing something new.</p></section><section class="reading-section"><h2>Stand graphics: include in the brief</h2><ul><li>Which kit you’d like to use, and any graphics you can reuse.</li><li>Venue dimensions, supplier artwork templates and display restrictions.</li><li>Audience, key messages and draft content.</li><li>Who reviews the artwork, the supplier deadline and the event organiser contacts.</li></ul></section><section class="reading-section"><h2>Merchandise: include in the brief</h2><ul><li>Why the item is useful for the audience.</li><li>Stock or an existing design that could be reused.</li><li>Quantity, budget, destination and use date.</li><li>Supplier requirements, material choices and who reviews the artwork.</li></ul></section><nav class="section-next" aria-label="More in Events"><div class="section-next-head"><h2>More in Events</h2><a class="related-all" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Events Support')">Plan event materials <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="related-grid"></div></nav>
