<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Typography</span><p>Use Noto Sans for the SKAO identity, with Verdana as the fallback.</p></div><a href="https://fonts.google.com/noto/specimen/Noto+Sans" class="button">Open Noto Sans at Google Fonts <span class="arr arr-out" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><section class="reading-section"><h2>Which weight to use</h2><ul><li><strong>Noto Sans Light</strong>: headlines, body text and long paragraphs.</li><li><strong>Noto Sans Medium</strong>: emphasis within body copy and bold headlines.</li><li><strong>Noto Sans Regular and Bold</strong>: small type, text over backgrounds, or where Light becomes hard to read.</li><li><strong>Noto Mono</strong>: technical text, metrics and footnotes, used sparingly.</li><li><strong>Verdana</strong>: the fallback when Noto Sans is not available.</li></ul></section><section class="reading-section"><h2>Use in your work</h2><ul><li>Follow the template’s existing text styles where available.</li><li>Use your organisation’s approved installation route on a managed device.</li><li>Check the font in the exported or shared file, particularly when moving between applications.</li></ul></section><aside class="next-step"><div><h2>Can’t install the font?</h2><p>Use the fallback and ask for help through your usual IT support route.</p></div><a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Colour Palette and Typography')" class="text-link">Return to typography guidance</a></aside><nav class="page-pager" aria-label="Previous and next in Brand"><a class="pager-prev" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Partner logos')" rel="prev"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span>Partner logos</a><a class="pager-next" href="$link.page('CRH', 'SKAO Brand Book')" rel="next">SKAO Brand Book<span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></nav><nav class="section-next" aria-label="More in Brand"><div class="section-next-head"><h2>More in Brand</h2><a class="related-all" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Brand Guidelines')">Brand guidance <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="related-grid"><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'SKAO Brand Book')"><strong>SKAO Brand Book</strong><span>The Brand Book is the detailed source for visual identity rules.</span></a><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Logo Usage and Downloads')"><strong>Using the SKAO logo</strong><span>Use official artwork, preserve its proportions and give it space.</span></a><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Colour Palette and Typography')"><strong>Colours and typography</strong><span>Official values from the SKAO Brand Book (March 2022). Copy what you need: hex or RGB for screen, CMYK or Pantone for print.</span></a></div></nav>
